00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:16,980
Now, that's a fresh ride.

267
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:20,280
Well, too bad the driver's a major dweeb.

268
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:22,460
Anyone can have a car like that if their daddy's loaded like his.

269
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:23,820
He's coming this way.

270
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:25,240
Be cool.

271
00:10:29,050 --> 00:10:29,650
Hey, guys.

272
00:10:30,050 --> 00:10:31,150
What do you think of my automobile?

273
00:10:31,790 --> 00:10:32,810
Isn't it bad to the bone?

274
00:10:32,970 --> 00:10:33,190
Word.

275
00:10:34,030 --> 00:10:38,330
The ladies are going to be lining up to get with you when they see you driving around in that car.

276
00:10:38,830 --> 00:10:39,590
You really think so?

277
00:10:39,870 --> 00:10:40,210
For sure.

278
00:10:40,970 --> 00:10:41,090
Awesome.

279
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:42,920
Psyche.

280
00:10:43,250 --> 00:10:44,390
You totally fell for it.

281
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:46,090
You're a real scumbag, Charlie.

282
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:49,590
When I do the nasty with the prom queen, we'll see who has the last laugh.

283
00:10:50,110 --> 00:10:51,090
Dude, don't have a cow.

284
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:56,760
Okay.

285
00:10:56,760 --> 00:11:00,500
So, Marco, when I was listening to the dialogue this time, I heard a really cool word.

286
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:03,120
They said, psyche.

287
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:04,120
Right.

288
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:09,600
And this was a very popular thing during the 80s when you would say to somebody, Psych.

289
00:11:09,600 --> 00:11:12,200
So this is like saying just kidding, right?

290
00:11:12,280 --> 00:11:13,280
Just kidding, right.

291
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:15,360
So you would say, oh, Erica, I really like your hat.

292
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:16,260
Oh, thank you.

293
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:17,820
Psych, that hat is terrible.

294
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:18,580
Oh.

295
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:19,820
Right?

296
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:21,320
So that's how you would use it.

297
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:30,640
You would give somebody a compliment or you would lie to somebody and then tell them, Psych, and then like tell them the truth like, oh, that hat is terrible or I was just kidding.

298
00:11:31,640 --> 00:11:32,640
Okay.

299
00:11:32,640 --> 00:11:33,640
So, psyche.

300
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:34,640
That was a phrase.

301
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:38,240
It was very, very popular and when I was in school, we would use it as well.

302
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:39,740
We would psych each other out.

303
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:41,380
So do we still use this phrase today?

304
00:11:41,990 --> 00:11:43,210
I don't think we use it today.

305
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:44,440
I don't think it's cool anymore.

306
00:11:44,510 --> 00:11:46,690
Well, if you'd use it, it's kind of like you're joking, right?

307
00:11:46,950 --> 00:11:47,170
Yeah.

308
00:11:47,250 --> 00:11:48,810
And I think it would make people laugh.

309
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:50,480
Like, you know, it's pretty funny.

310
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:51,480
Yeah.

311
00:11:51,480 --> 00:11:53,000
You're joking about how you're a little bit old-fashioned.

312
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,000
Exactly.

313
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,000
Yeah.

